[h3]Universal Translators and Calibrated Terminals[/h3]

Colony broadcast update: Following an incident where Meep attempted to explain temperature limits to Nisbet by frantically waving a red-hot Obsidian boulder, colony management has equipped the Printing Pod with universal linguistic frequency modulators.

Simultaneously, colony engineers have completely overhauled the Mod Options terminal. Gone are the clunky, fogged-up analog dials - the entire dialog has been rebuilt with crisp digital readouts, real-time temperature previews, and calibrated unit switches.

[b]Changes[/b]
[list]
[*] [b]Multilingual Printing Pod (18 Languages):[/b] Temperature limits, side-screens, and options are now fully fluent in Chinese (Simplified & Traditional), Czech, French, German, Greek, Hungarian, Italian, Japanese, Korean, Polish, Portuguese & Brazilian Portuguese, Spanish, Thai, Turkish, Ukrainian, and Vietnamese. Duplicants no longer need to interpret thermal limits through frantic interpretive dance.
[*] [b]Modernized Colony Options Terminal:[/b] Rebuilt the mod settings screen into a dedicated, themed dialog. Features real-time temperature previews with instant C, F, and K unit conversions matching colony preferences, a one-click Reset to Defaults button, and full keyboard navigation (Tab between fields, Enter to commit, Escape to dismiss).
[*] [b]Late-Game Performance:[/b] Duplicants no longer survey every item on the asteroid before deciding where to set down a rock. Each eligible building now keeps its allowed temperature range on file, and errands are checked against the file instead of the asteroid.
[*] [b]Thermo Sensor-Grade Interface Overhaul:[/b] Distinct "At least" and "Below" thresholds that never fight each other, engraved unit labels outside the input fields, a dedicated Clear button, live status readout with warning highlights, and keyboard support.
[*] [b]Unjammed Colony Steering (No More Swallowed WASD):[/b] Panning (WASD), pausing (Space), and emergency Escape are never captured by overzealous temperature boxes. Duplicants may still sprint into a magma pool, but at least you can now pan over to watch them do it.
[*] [b]Errand and Warning Decisions:[/b] Delivery assignments and the temperature-aware "Lacks Resources" warning keep pace as the colony spreads across asteroids, space stations, and rockets.
[*] [b]Fast Track Compatibility:[/b] Runs smoothly alongside current releases of Peter Han's [url=https://github.com/peterhaneve/ONIMods/tree/main/FastTrack][i]Fast Track[/i][/url] when present, with zero overhead when running on the standard game engine.
[*] [b]Fresh Start on Every Load:[/b] Returning to the main menu sweeps out all background tracking. A bin in one colony can no longer be haunted by the limits of a colony you abandoned.
[*] [b]Support Reports:[/b] If something goes thermally sideways, generate a privacy-safe diagnostic report directly from the Options dialog. It stays on your machine.
[/list]

[b]Notes[/b]
[list]
[*] [b]Your Bins Are Safe:[/b] Existing temperature limits, blueprint construction settings, copied building settings, and saved colonies carry over untouched. The filing cabinet survived the renovation.
[/list]

[b]Known Issues[/b]
[list]
[*] Duplicants still have opinions about which rock is nearest. Unrelated.
[/list]

Every colony is its own lovingly overcomplicated thermodynamic incident, so results will vary. No Duplicants were asked to benchmark molten tungsten.
